  "articleBody": "Hiring a residential painter can be exciting, but some common pitfalls can turn your dream project into a headache. Here are a few mistakes to steer clear of:\n\n1.  **Accepting a vague estimate:** Make sure your estimate specifies everything – product brands, number of coats, and all prep work. If it's not written down, it might not be included.\n\n2.  **Skipping on cleanup clarity:** Don't assume cleanup is part of the deal. Confirm who is responsible for removing debris and cleaning up the workspace at the end of each day and the project.\n\n3.  **Forgetting about insurance and references:** Always verify your painter’s insurance and ask for references. This protects you in case of accidents and gives you insight into their past work.\n\n4.  **Not confirming warranty terms:** Understand what kind of warranty is offered on the work. A good warranty provides peace of mind long after the paint dries.\n\n5.  **Overlooking detailed surface repair:** If your walls need a lot of TLC, don't assume basic patching. Discuss how cracks, holes, and other imperfections will be addressed before painting. HH Remodeling LLC always emphasizes clear communication and detailed quotes to prevent these common issues, ensuring you know exactly what to expect.",
